From: provider-openfga maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] fix(authorization model): remove from state when it no longer exists

The store resource and the relationship tuple resource both drop themselves
from the Terraform state when OpenFGA answers that they are gone, so that
Terraform plans a create instead of failing. The authorization model resource
does not, even though apierror.IsStatusNotFound already special-cases
`authorization_model_not_found`, so a refresh of a model that does not exist
fails the whole run:

    Error: Client Error
    Unable to read authorization model, got error: GET validation error for
    ReadAuthorizationModel GET with body
    {"code":"authorization_model_not_found","message":"Authorization Model
    '...' not found"}

That breaks `terraform plan` after a model is deleted out of band, and it
breaks any tool that refreshes a resource before creating it, which is how
Crossplane providers generated with Upjet observe a resource.

This mirrors the store resource's Read exactly.

diff --git a/internal/provider/authorizationmodel/authorization_model_resource.go b/internal/provider/authorizationmodel/authorization_model_resource.go
index 42c5e05..85197b2 100644
--- a/internal/provider/authorizationmodel/authorization_model_resource.go
+++ b/internal/provider/authorizationmodel/authorization_model_resource.go
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@ import (
 	"github.com/hashicorp/terraform-plugin-framework/types"
 
 	"github.com/openfga/go-sdk/client"
+
+	internalError "github.com/openfga/terraform-provider-openfga/internal/apierror"
 )
 
 // Ensure provider defined types fully satisfy framework interfaces.
@@ -123,6 +125,15 @@ func (r *AuthorizationModelResource) Read(ctx context.Context, req resource.Read
 
 	authorizationModelModel, err := r.client.ReadAuthorizationModel(ctx, state.StoreId.ValueString(), state.AuthorizationModelModel)
 	if err != nil {
+		if internalError.IsStatusNotFound(err) {
+			resp.Diagnostics.AddWarning(
+				"Authorization model not found",
+				fmt.Sprintf("Authorization model %q no longer exists; removing from state.", state.Id.ValueString()),
+			)
+			resp.State.RemoveResource(ctx)
+			return
+		}
+
 		resp.Diagnostics.AddError("Client Error", fmt.Sprintf("Unable to read authorization model, got error: %s", err))
 		return
 	}
